                                                "sense_id": "d3b52af6-7e4d-3c4f-b9fc-e52e380576be",
                                                "text": "Polyploidy and hybridisation are important evolutionary forces shaping plant genomes and underlying the huge angiosperm diversity. Both can confer evolutionary advantages [44–46] attributed to the plasticity of plant genomes and to increased genetic variability, generating individuals capable of exploiting new niches [47]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1c4f58c-e016-43cb-9688-7aa6eb5a704d",
                                                "sense_id": "d3b52af6-7e4d-3c4f-b9fc-e52e380576be",
                                                "text": "In situ hybridisations were performed on devitellinised embryos still wrapped around the yolk and on embryos with the yolk dissected away."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
